  "body": "A script starts `camcraft-ui some.camproj` from a background process. The window takes the foreground. The script cannot prevent this.\n\n## What happens (CamCraft 0.25.0, Windows 11)\n- The launcher sets STARTUPINFO `wShowWindow` to `SW_SHOWMINNOACTIVE` (7) or `SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE` (4). This has no effect.\n- The window is visible and not minimized at about 40 ms after launch.\n- The window is the foreground window from that time.\n\nI polled with EnumWindows, IsWindowVisible, GetWindowRect and GetForegroundWindow.\n\n## Cause (found in the code)\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell_window.rs` (`init_gpu`) creates the window with default attributes. In winit 0.30.13 a visible, active window is shown with `ShowWindow(SW_SHOW)` (`window_state.rs`, `apply_diff`).\n- The same function then calls `window.focus_window()`. On Windows this sends a synthetic Alt key press to get past the foreground lock, so the lock timeout does not matter.\n- Nothing in the program reads the launcher's show state.\n\n## Proposal\nTwo new start options in the `cli_options` table:\n- `--no-activate`: create the window inactive and do not call `focus_window()`. The window shows, and the focused window keeps the focus.\n- `--minimized`: the same, and the window starts minimized. It covers no other window.\n\nThe default does not change. A separate step could read STARTUPINFO on Windows. That is a larger change, so it is not proposed here.\n\nA patch is ready on a branch. It has unit tests for the parser and the window attributes. I also checked both options with the project on the command line, from a process started by Task Scheduler (not from a terminal). The window was never the foreground window, and it did not take the focus when the project finished loading. `--minimized` gave a minimized window. Not tested: macOS, Linux.\n\nIs this the wanted shape?\n",
